// Rule: [T1564.004] Btr Reforged - Btr CLI Driver Dat Ads
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1564.004
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Required telemetry: WindowsEvent
// Purpose: Proactive validation of the current BTR_CLI feedback-stream artifact on Microsoft Defender remediation drivers.
// Logic: Evaluate WindowsEvent for btr cli driver dat ads using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A .dat named stream was created on a .sys file and requires raw-event, driver and privilege investigation.
// A match does not prove: BTR.sys abuse, successful kernel actions, Defender neutralization or attacker presence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Validation query - Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Prerequisite: Sysmon Event ID 15 from Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational
// collected into WindowsEvent through an AMA DCR or Windows Event Forwarding.
// Evidence: Check Point observed BTR_CLI writing its feedback report to a
// secondary .dat ADS on the .sys driver. The current legitimate Defender
// workflow writes feedback as a standalone file under RebootActions instead.
WindowsEvent
| where Provider == "Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon"
| where Channel == "Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| where EventID == 15
| extend TargetFilename = tostring(EventData.TargetFilename)
| where TargetFilename contains ".sys:"
    and TargetFilename endswith ".dat"
| project
    TimeGenerated, Computer, EventRecordId, Provider, Channel, EventID,
    TargetFilename, EventData, RawEventData, SystemProcessId, SystemUserId,
    Correlation, _ResourceId
| order by TimeGenerated desc
